-- title:
--   Away-from-v units of an Eichler order span the algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\bar r$ be a prime and let $a_1,b_1$ be rationals such that the quaternion algebra $H=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`, that is: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the base change $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $\bar r$ lies in the prime ideal of $v$. Let $N$ be a natural number and let $R_1\subseteq H$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R_1=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ each maximal among the orders containing it, with the relative index of $R_1$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive groups equal to $N$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq\bar r$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideal contains $r$. Consider the subgroup $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_1\,v\le H^\times$ consisting of those units of $H$ whose image in $(H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w)^\times$, under the map induced by $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$, lies in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$ (the units of $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ having both themselves and their inverse in `localBox R₁ w`), for every height-one prime $w\neq v$. The conclusion is that the $\mathbb{Q}$-linear span in $H$ of the underlying elements of this subgroup is the whole of $H$.
--
--   This is the spanning statement extracted from strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite quaternion algebra away from the place $v$ above $r$, at which $H$ is split: the $S$-units of an Eichler order are Zariski-dense enough to generate $H$ linearly. It is used in [`QuaternionAlgebra.exists_eq_smul_one_of_forall_mem_awayUnits_commute`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.exists_eq_smul_one_of_forall_mem_awayUnits_commute), where an element commuting with all away-from-$v$ units is forced to be a rational scalar; the proof here invokes [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_mem_awayUnits_mul_ne_mul_of_isDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_mem_awayUnits_mul_ne_mul_of_isDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt), the existence of a non-commuting pair of such units.
